WEEK 1 | Commit 5

CHANGES:
- Updated FeedbackRequest Pydantic schema: session_id and message_id now Optional
- Changed FeedbackReport SQLAlchemy model: message_id column now nullable=True

DETAILS:
- Before: session_id was required (UUID) in FeedbackRequest schema
- Before: message_id did not exist in FeedbackRequest, was hardcoded in router
- Before: FeedbackReport.message_id was nullable=False in database, preventing null inserts
- After: session_id is Optional[UUID] = None, can be omitted for general feedback
- After: message_id is Optional[UUID] = None, added to schema with proper type annotation
- After: FeedbackReport.message_id column changed to nullable=True in database model
- This enables the navbar FeedbackModal to submit general feedback without any chat context
- Message-specific reports from the chat ReportModal still work by providing message_id
- Updated issue_type field description to list all valid categories

